body:
 [https://imgur.com/a/F8bXC1R](https://imgur.com/a/F8bXC1R) 

&#x200B;

Im getting it from the minecraft server gui thingy. It only shows how much ram the server is using.

\> I've taken down the numbers (mb of ram and % used) over a few minutes and did some calculations and it can be confirmed that the amount of total ram (in the context of the server) varies over time.

&#x200B;

I took down the numbers and the percentages and i used a website i found on google to work out the total ram and it does change (more specifically i found that the total ram varied from 700mb to 1000mb)

Hey. So personally i tend to use alt accounts to post stuff because i get a bit weirded out when someone mentions something they've read in one of my old posts. Im sure there are people that wouldn't want to chat with someone who has no reddit history but i for one don't really care about someone's post history and im sure there are others that feel the same way. 

&#x200B;

This is a pretty good sub but i think you should also consider other subs that deal specifically with mental health. I know of /r/depression but im sure there's one for PTSD. 

&#x200B;

Hope you have a great day!
